  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`src/sites.rs#fn[validate_review]` is a site. It takes a parameter named `errors` and collects validation errors in it. Each check pushes a message that begins with `label`, the evidence file. The message then names the failed check and gives the recorded and expected values where they are available.\n\nI judged each early-exit match:\n- **The `return` after the failed `fs::read_to_string`, the `return` after the failed `serde_json::from_str`, and the `return` when the value is not a JSON object.** Each one is a file-level read, parse, or shape failure. The requirement allows that to count as one failed check that reports only its first problem. Every later check reads the file's contents, so none of them could run without it.\n- **The `return` after the failed `application_fields` decode.** Later checks need the decoded application fields, so they depend on its result. `check_native` runs before it and does not repeat it. `check_native` states that application fields are reported by the application validators, and it reports only the SDK header and dependency freshness. So the two do not report one failure twice.\n- **The `?` operators on `fixme.get(\"item\")?` and `fixme.get(\"commentary\")?`, with their `.as_str()?` calls.** They sit inside a closure that yields `Option`. They do not leave the function. A `None` becomes a single \"fixmes must be an array of objects...\" error, and every later check still runs.\n- **The final `return` when `inputs` is missing or not an array.** `array_field` has already reported that problem once. Only the input-dependent checks follow it, and they cannot run without `inputs`. All the independent checks come before it.\n\nThe independent checks all run regardless of earlier failures. These are the key set, the requirement, file and item fields, the recorded queries, the fixmes, `applies`, the determination, the rationale, the `applies`/determination consistency rule, the determination-specific fixme validation, and the input checks. I found no check that is skipped without a dependency on a failed check, and no failure reported twice. `validate_review` meets the obligations.",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "file": "src/sites.rs",
      "item": "fn[validate_review]",
      "hash": "65d812f5850d755f0089829889b5d713acef0082921f8ef95015a6effe7e395b"
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.ci.errors",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.ci.errors"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::::{req} errors",
        "Repository validation MUST continue after a failed check and report every failed",
        "check it finds in one run, each as a {term}`requirements.ci.validation_error`.",
        "This is a convention for every validation error; the requirement for each check",
        "states which conditions that check reports. A file that cannot be parsed, such as",
        "a malformed `habeas.toml`, `book.toml`, or evidence file, is one failed check:",
        "its error MAY report only the first parse or decoding problem in that file, and",
        "checks that do not depend on its contents MUST still run.",
        "",
        "The code that sequences the repository's checks carries out the first paragraph.",
        "A repository-validation function that collects validation errors MUST hold them",
        "in a parameter or local variable named `errors`, and a function with such a",
        "variable is a site below; authoring code that collects errors only to abort is",
        "not one. After one of its checks fails, a site MUST still run every later check",
        "that does not depend on the failed check's result, including later checks in the",
        "same loop iteration, and MUST NOT report one failure twice.",
        "",
        "::::{sites} error_accumulators",
        "```yaml",
        "language: rust",
        "paths: [src, crates/trust-but-verify/src]",
        "exclude: [src/authoring/inputs.rs, src/authoring/tools.rs]",
        "rule:",
        "  kind: function_item",
        "  has:",
        "    stopBy: { kind: function_item }",
        "    any:",
        "      - kind: parameter",
        "        has: { field: pattern, regex: \"^errors$\" }",
        "      - kind: let_declaration",
        "        has: { field: pattern, regex: \"^errors$\" }",
        "  not:",
        "    inside:",
        "      stopBy: end",
        "      kind: mod_item",
        "      has: { field: name, regex: \"^tests$\" }",
        "match:",
        "  - \"fn check(value: &str, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\"",
        "  - |",
        "    fn run() {",
        "        let mut errors: BTreeSet<String> = BTreeSet::new();",
        "        check(\"\", &mut errors);",
        "    }",
        "no_match:",
        "  - \"fn check(value: &str, discovery_errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\"",
        "  - |",
        "    fn run() {",
        "        let mut problems = Vec::new();",
        "        check(\"\", &mut problems);",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    mod tests {",
        "        fn check(errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}",
        "    }",
        "```",
        "::::",
        "",
        "::::{violations} early_exits",
        "```yaml",
        "language: rust",
        "paths: [src, crates/trust-but-verify/src]",
        "within: error_accumulators",
        "rule:",
        "  any:",
        "    - kind: try_expression",
        "    - kind: return_expression",
        "    - kind: continue_expression",
        "    - kind: break_expression",
        "match:",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(v: &Value, errors: &mut Vec<String>) -> Option<u8> {",
        "        let n = v.as_u64()?;",
        "        if v.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "        Some(n as u8)",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(items: &[Value], errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        for item in items {",
        "            if !item.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); continue; }",
        "            if item.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "        }",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(v: &Value, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        if !v.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); return; }",
        "        if v.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(items: &[Value], errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        for item in items {",
        "            if !item.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); break; }",
        "        }",
        "        if items.is_empty() { errors.push(\"empty\".into()); }",
        "    }",
        "no_match:",
        "  - |",
        "    fn parse(v: &Value) -> Option<u8> {",
        "        let n = v.as_u64()?;",
        "        Some(n as u8)",
        "    }",
        "```",
        "::::",
        ":::::"
      ]
    },
